            "review_text": "Explore51261543715\n1 contribution\n0\nA library that lives down a canyon\nMar 2026 • Solo\nI didn’t think there was a library cafe in the alleyway that well-stocked. The towering bookshelves surrounded by ceilings create a very special space, perfect for those seeking a quiet spot. I’ve tried the intricate Grape Meadows, the quirky combination of cafe phin and the long-stayed fat cat salt. The staff here is exquisite at attentive to small needs like an electrical drive without disturbing guests.\nRead more\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten March 9, 2026",
